/-!
# The relative Grothendieck group of a functor

For a functor `T : C ⥤ D` from a category with zero morphisms and binary biproducts to a category
with zero morphisms, preserving zero morphisms and binary biproducts (an additive functor between
additive categories, in the intended application), the relative group `TauCeti.RelativeK0 T`,
written `K₀(T)`, is the abelian group generated by the triples `(P, α, Q)` of objects `P`, `Q`
of `C` and an isomorphism `α : T P ≅ T Q` in `D`, subject to

* isomorphism invariance: `(P, α, Q) = (P', α', Q')` whenever there are isomorphisms `f : P ≅ P'`
  and `g : Q ≅ Q'` with `α' ∘ T f = T g ∘ α`;
* the direct-sum relation `(P ⊞ P', α ⊞ α', Q ⊞ Q') = (P, α, Q) + (P', α', Q')`;
* the composition relation `(P, β ∘ α, S) = (P, α, Q) + (Q, β, S)`.

The triples and the isomorphisms between them are exactly the objects and isomorphisms of Mathlib's
categorical pullback `T ⊡ T`, so `K₀(T)` is the Grothendieck group of `T ⊡ T` presented by the
direct-sum and composition relations, built with Tau Ceti's presentation engine
`TauCeti.PresentedK0`; isomorphism invariance is then automatic, and `K₀(T)` lives in any
universe `w` in which `C` is essentially small and `D` is locally small.

`K₀(T)` is the relative term of the exact sequence `K₁(D) → K₀(T) → K₀(C) → K₀(D)` of a cofinal
functor, and applied to base change `Proj(R) ⥤ Proj(R/I)` it gives the relative group `K₀(R, I)`
of a ring and a two-sided ideal. This file constructs the group, its
universal property and its two structure maps: the difference map
`TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0 : K₀(T) → K₀(C)`, `[(P, α, Q)] ↦ [P] - [Q]`, into the split
Grothendieck group of `C`, and the maps `TauCeti.RelativeK0.map` induced by commuting squares of
functors.

The presentation uses only direct sums, but when `D` is preadditive with binary biproducts it
already satisfies the relation for split short exact sequences of triples
(`TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq`): if
`γ : T (P₁ ⊞ P₂) ≅ T (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)` is triangular, restricting to `α₁` on the first summand and
inducing `α₂` on the second, then `(P₁ ⊞ P₂, γ, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) = (P₁, α₁, Q₁) + (P₂, α₂, Q₂)`, whatever
its off-diagonal block. That block need not come from a morphism of `C`: the unipotent
automorphism it defines becomes a commutator after adding a summand
(`CategoryTheory.Biprod.unipotentLower_biprod_eq_commutatorElement`), and commutators have trivial
class because the automorphisms of a fixed `T P` contribute additively
(`TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_trans_commutatorElement_trans`). This is the additivity that Weibel's
presentation of `K₀(T)` imposes along short exact sequences of triples, for those sequences which
split, as all short exact sequences of finitely generated projective modules do.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleBiprod x y`: the direct sum of two triples, with its isomorphisms
  `TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleBiprodMapIso` (functoriality), `TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleBiprodComm`,
  `TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleBiprodAssoc` and `TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleBiprodReflIso` (the sum of
  two identity triples).
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0 T`: the relative group, with class map `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.AdditiveInvariant T G`: the functions on triples that factor through
  `K₀(T)`, and `TauCeti.RelativeK0.lift` the homomorphism they induce.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0`: the difference map `K₀(T) → K₀(C)`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleMap` and `TauCeti.RelativeK0.map`: the functor of triples and the
  homomorphism `K₀(T) → K₀(T')` induced by functors `F : C ⥤ C'`, `G : D ⥤ D'` and a natural
  isomorphism `T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T'`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero`: when every object of `D` is zero, the difference
  map is an isomorphism `K₀(T) ≃+ K₀(C)`, with inverse `[P] ↦ [(P, 0, 0)]`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_tripleBiprod` and `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_trans`: the defining
  relations, with their consequences `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_refl` (`(P, id, P) = 0`),
  `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_symm` (`(Q, α⁻¹, P) = -(P, α, Q)`) and `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_mapIso`
  (`(P, T γ, Q) = 0` for every isomorphism `γ : P ≅ Q`).
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.exists_eq_of`: every element of `K₀(T)` is the class of a single triple.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_trans_commutatorElement_trans`: commutators of automorphisms have
  trivial class.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq`: the relation for triangular
  isomorphisms, with the unipotent case
  `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_eq_zero_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.liftEquiv`: the universal property.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.splitK0Map_comp_toSplitK0_eq_zero`: the composite `K₀(T) → K₀(C) → K₀(D)`
  vanishes.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.subsingleton_of_fullyFaithful`: `K₀(T) = 0` for a fully faithful `T`; in
  particular `K₀(𝟭 C) = 0`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0_comp_map`: the difference maps are natural in commuting squares.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.map_id` and `TauCeti.RelativeK0.map_comp`: the maps induced by commuting
  squares are functorial, for the identity square and for vertically pasted squares.

## References

* Charles A. Weibel, *The K-book: An Introduction to Algebraic K-theory*, Chapter II,
  Definition 2.10 (the relative group `K₀(f)` of a ring map and `K₀(R, I)`) and Exercise 2.17
  (the group `K₀(T)` of a cofinal functor and its exact sequence).
* Charles A. Weibel, *The K-book*, Chapter III, Lemma 1.3.2 (the commutator identity for
  elementary matrices behind the triangular relation).
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Limits.CategoricalPullback ZeroObject

universe w w' w'' v v' v'' v''' v₅ v₆ u u' u'' u''' u₅ u₆

section Triples

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [HasZeroMorphisms D]
  (T : C ⥤ D) [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T]

namespace RelativeK0

/-- The direct sum of two triples `x = (P, α, Q)` and `y = (P', α', Q')`: the triple
`(P ⊞ P', α ⊞ α', Q ⊞ Q')`, where `α ⊞ α'` is read through the identifications
`T (X ⊞ Y) ≅ T X ⊞ T Y`. Its isomorphism is characterized by
`TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleBiprod_iso_hom_map_fst` and
`TauCeti.RelativeK0.tripleBiprod_iso_hom_map_snd`. -/
-- The body is exposed: the type of the isomorphism of a triple depends on its two ends, so the
-- characteristic equations of the isomorphism need the ends of the direct sum definitionally.
@[expose]
noncomputable def tripleBiprod (x y : T ⊡ T) : T ⊡ T :=
  letI := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
  { fst := x.fst ⊞ y.fst
    snd := x.snd ⊞ y.snd
    iso := T.mapBiprod _ _ ≪≫ biprod.mapIso x.iso y.iso ≪≫ (T.mapBiprod _ _).symm }

variable {T}

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprod_fst (x y : T ⊡ T) : (tripleBiprod T x y).fst = (x.fst ⊞ y.fst) := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprod_snd (x y : T ⊡ T) : (tripleBiprod T x y).snd = (x.snd ⊞ y.snd) := (rfl)

/-- The first component of the isomorphism of a direct sum of triples. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma tripleBiprod_iso_hom_map_fst (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprod T x y).iso.hom ≫ T.map (biprod.fst : x.snd ⊞ y.snd ⟶ x.snd) =
      T.map biprod.fst ≫ x.iso.hom := by
  have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
  dsimp only [tripleBiprod]
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, biprod.mapIso_hom, Category.assoc,
    Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst, biprod.map_fst, Functor.mapBiprod_hom, biprod.lift_fst_assoc]

/-- The second component of the isomorphism of a direct sum of triples. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma tripleBiprod_iso_hom_map_snd (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprod T x y).iso.hom ≫ T.map (biprod.snd : x.snd ⊞ y.snd ⟶ y.snd) =
      T.map biprod.snd ≫ y.iso.hom := by
  have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
  dsimp only [tripleBiprod]
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, biprod.mapIso_hom, Category.assoc,
    Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd, biprod.map_snd, Functor.mapBiprod_hom, biprod.lift_snd_assoc]

/-! ### Isomorphisms of direct sums of triples

The isomorphism conditions below are proved with `tripleBiprod` unfolded, as in the two
characteristic lemmas above. The ends `(tripleBiprod T x y).fst` and `x.fst ⊞ y.fst` agree only
up to unfolding `tripleBiprod`, so `simp` cannot apply the characteristic lemmas to composites
whose objects are written one way and whose morphisms, such as `biprod.braiding`, the other. -/

/-- The direct sum of isomorphisms of triples `e : x ≅ x'` and `e' : y ≅ y'`, an isomorphism
`x ⊞ y ≅ x' ⊞ y'` whose two components are the direct sums of the components of `e` and `e'`. -/
noncomputable def tripleBiprodMapIso {x x' y y' : T ⊡ T} (e : x ≅ x') (e' : y ≅ y') :
    tripleBiprod T x y ≅ tripleBiprod T x' y' :=
  mkIso (biprod.mapIso (asIso e.hom.fst) (asIso e'.hom.fst))
    (biprod.mapIso (asIso e.hom.snd) (asIso e'.hom.snd)) (by
      have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
      dsimp only [tripleBiprod]
      refine Functor.map_biprod_hom_ext ?_ ?_ <;>
        simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, biprod.mapIso_hom,
          Functor.mapBiprod_hom, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd,
          biprod.map_fst, biprod.map_snd, biprod.lift_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_snd_assoc,
          ← T.map_comp_assoc, ← T.map_comp, asIso_hom] <;>
        simp only [T.map_comp, Category.assoc, Hom.w, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst_assoc,
          Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd_assoc, biprod.map_fst_assoc, biprod.map_snd_assoc,
          biprod.lift_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_snd_assoc])

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodMapIso_hom_fst {x x' y y' : T ⊡ T} (e : x ≅ x') (e' : y ≅ y') :
    (tripleBiprodMapIso e e').hom.fst = biprod.map e.hom.fst e'.hom.fst := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodMapIso_hom_snd {x x' y y' : T ⊡ T} (e : x ≅ x') (e' : y ≅ y') :
    (tripleBiprodMapIso e e').hom.snd = biprod.map e.hom.snd e'.hom.snd := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodMapIso_inv_fst {x x' y y' : T ⊡ T} (e : x ≅ x') (e' : y ≅ y') :
    (tripleBiprodMapIso e e').inv.fst = biprod.map (inv e.hom.fst) (inv e'.hom.fst) := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodMapIso_inv_snd {x x' y y' : T ⊡ T} (e : x ≅ x') (e' : y ≅ y') :
    (tripleBiprodMapIso e e').inv.snd = biprod.map (inv e.hom.snd) (inv e'.hom.snd) := (rfl)

/-- The direct sum of triples is commutative: `x ⊞ y ≅ y ⊞ x` through the braidings of both
components. -/
noncomputable def tripleBiprodComm (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    tripleBiprod T x y ≅ tripleBiprod T y x :=
  mkIso (biprod.braiding _ _) (biprod.braiding _ _) (by
    have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
    dsimp only [tripleBiprod]
    refine Functor.map_biprod_hom_ext ?_ ?_ <;>
      simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, biprod.mapIso_hom,
        Functor.mapBiprod_hom, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd,
        biprod.map_fst, biprod.map_snd, biprod.lift_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_snd_assoc,
        ← T.map_comp_assoc, ← T.map_comp, biprod.braiding_hom, biprod.lift_fst, biprod.lift_snd])

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodComm_hom_fst (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodComm x y).hom.fst = (biprod.braiding x.fst y.fst).hom := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodComm_hom_snd (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodComm x y).hom.snd = (biprod.braiding x.snd y.snd).hom := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodComm_inv_fst (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodComm x y).inv.fst = (biprod.braiding x.fst y.fst).inv := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodComm_inv_snd (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodComm x y).inv.snd = (biprod.braiding x.snd y.snd).inv := (rfl)

/-- The direct sum of triples is associative: `(x ⊞ y) ⊞ z ≅ x ⊞ (y ⊞ z)` through the
associators of both components. -/
noncomputable def tripleBiprodAssoc (x y z : T ⊡ T) :
    tripleBiprod T (tripleBiprod T x y) z ≅ tripleBiprod T x (tripleBiprod T y z) :=
  mkIso (biprod.associator _ _ _) (biprod.associator _ _ _) (by
    have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
    dsimp only [tripleBiprod]
    refine Functor.map_biprod_hom_ext ?_ (Functor.map_biprod_hom_ext ?_ ?_) <;>
      simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, biprod.mapIso_hom,
        Functor.mapBiprod_hom, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd,
        biprod.map_fst, biprod.map_snd, biprod.lift_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_snd_assoc] <;>
      simp only [← T.map_comp_assoc, ← T.map_comp, biprod.associator_hom, biprod.lift_fst,
        biprod.lift_snd, biprod.lift_snd_assoc] <;>
      simp only [Category.assoc, T.map_comp, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst,
        Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst_assoc, biprod.map_fst,
        biprod.map_snd, biprod.map_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_snd_assoc])

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodAssoc_hom_fst (x y z : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodAssoc x y z).hom.fst = (biprod.associator x.fst y.fst z.fst).hom := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodAssoc_hom_snd (x y z : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodAssoc x y z).hom.snd = (biprod.associator x.snd y.snd z.snd).hom := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodAssoc_inv_fst (x y z : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodAssoc x y z).inv.fst = (biprod.associator x.fst y.fst z.fst).inv := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodAssoc_inv_snd (x y z : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleBiprodAssoc x y z).inv.snd = (biprod.associator x.snd y.snd z.snd).inv := (rfl)

/-- The direct sum of the identity triples `(S, id, S)` and `(S', id, S')` is the identity triple
`(S ⊞ S', id, S ⊞ S')`. -/
noncomputable def tripleBiprodReflIso (S S' : C) :
    tripleBiprod T ⟨S, S, Iso.refl _⟩ ⟨S', S', Iso.refl _⟩ ≅ ⟨S ⊞ S', S ⊞ S', Iso.refl _⟩ :=
  mkIso (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (by
    have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
    dsimp only [tripleBiprod]
    refine Functor.map_biprod_hom_ext ?_ ?_ <;>
      simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, biprod.mapIso_hom, Iso.refl_hom,
        Functor.mapBiprod_hom, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd,
        biprod.map_fst, biprod.map_snd, T.map_id, Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id,
        biprod.lift_fst, biprod.lift_snd])

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodReflIso_hom_fst (S S' : C) :
    (tripleBiprodReflIso (T := T) S S').hom.fst = 𝟙 (S ⊞ S') := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodReflIso_hom_snd (S S' : C) :
    (tripleBiprodReflIso (T := T) S S').hom.snd = 𝟙 (S ⊞ S') := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodReflIso_inv_fst (S S' : C) :
    (tripleBiprodReflIso (T := T) S S').inv.fst = 𝟙 (S ⊞ S') := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma tripleBiprodReflIso_inv_snd (S S' : C) :
    (tripleBiprodReflIso (T := T) S S').inv.snd = 𝟙 (S ⊞ S') := (rfl)

end RelativeK0

variable [EssentiallySmall.{w} C] [LocallySmall.{w} D]

namespace RelativeK0

/-- The direct-sum relation `[(P ⊞ P', α ⊞ α', Q ⊞ Q')] - [(P, α, Q)] - [(P', α', Q')]`. -/
noncomputable def biprodRelation (x y : T ⊡ T) : FreeAddCommGroup (ObjectCode (T ⊡ T)) :=
  freeOf (tripleBiprod T x y) - freeOf x - freeOf y

/-- The defining equation of `TauCeti.RelativeK0.biprodRelation`. -/
lemma biprodRelation_def (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    biprodRelation T x y = freeOf (tripleBiprod T x y) - freeOf x - freeOf y := (rfl)

/-- The composition relation `[(P, β ∘ α, S)] - [(P, α, Q)] - [(Q, β, S)]`. -/
noncomputable def transRelation {P Q S : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S) :
    FreeAddCommGroup (ObjectCode (T ⊡ T)) :=
  freeOf (⟨P, S, α ≪≫ β⟩ : T ⊡ T) - freeOf (⟨P, Q, α⟩ : T ⊡ T) - freeOf (⟨Q, S, β⟩ : T ⊡ T)

omit [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C] [HasZeroMorphisms D] [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms]
  [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T] in
/-- The defining equation of `TauCeti.RelativeK0.transRelation`. -/
lemma transRelation_def {P Q S : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S) :
    transRelation T α β = freeOf (⟨P, S, α ≪≫ β⟩ : T ⊡ T) - freeOf (⟨P, Q, α⟩ : T ⊡ T) -
      freeOf (⟨Q, S, β⟩ : T ⊡ T) := (rfl)

/-- The family of direct-sum and composition relations presenting the relative group. -/
def relations : Set (FreeAddCommGroup (ObjectCode (T ⊡ T))) :=
  {r | (∃ x y : T ⊡ T, r = biprodRelation T x y) ∨
    ∃ (P Q S : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S), r = transRelation T α β}

/-- Membership in the family of relations presenting the relative group. -/
@[simp]
lemma mem_relations_iff {r : FreeAddCommGroup (ObjectCode (T ⊡ T))} :
    r ∈ relations T ↔ (∃ x y : T ⊡ T, r = biprodRelation T x y) ∨
      ∃ (P Q S : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S),
        r = transRelation T α β := (Iff.rfl)

lemma biprodRelation_mem_relations (x y : T ⊡ T) : biprodRelation T x y ∈ relations T :=
  (mem_relations_iff T).2 (Or.inl ⟨x, y, rfl⟩)

lemma transRelation_mem_relations {P Q S : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S) :
    transRelation T α β ∈ relations T :=
  (mem_relations_iff T).2 (Or.inr ⟨P, Q, S, α, β, rfl⟩)

end RelativeK0

/-- The relative Grothendieck group `K₀(T)` of a functor `T` preserving zero morphisms and binary
biproducts: the free abelian group on the isomorphism classes of triples `(P, α, Q)` with
`α : T P ≅ T Q`, modulo the direct-sum relation
`(P ⊞ P', α ⊞ α', Q ⊞ Q') = (P, α, Q) + (P', α', Q')` and the composition relation
`(P, β ∘ α, S) = (P, α, Q) + (Q, β, S)`. -/
def RelativeK0 : Type w := PresentedK0 (RelativeK0.relations T)

noncomputable instance : AddCommGroup (RelativeK0 T) :=
  inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup (PresentedK0 (RelativeK0.relations T)))

namespace RelativeK0

variable {T}

/-- The class of a triple `(P, α, Q)` in the relative group. -/
noncomputable def of (x : T ⊡ T) : RelativeK0 T := PresentedK0.of x

/-- Isomorphic triples have the same class. -/
lemma of_congr {x y : T ⊡ T} (e : x ≅ y) : (of x : RelativeK0 T) = of y :=
  PresentedK0.of_congr e

/-- The direct-sum relation: the class of a direct sum of triples is the sum of the classes. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_tripleBiprod (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (of (tripleBiprod T x y) : RelativeK0 T) = of x + of y := by
  have h : (PresentedK0.mk (biprodRelation T x y) : PresentedK0 (relations T)) = 0 :=
    PresentedK0.mk_eq_zero_of_mem (biprodRelation_mem_relations T x y)
  rw [biprodRelation_def, map_sub, map_sub, PresentedK0.mk_freeOf, PresentedK0.mk_freeOf,
    PresentedK0.mk_freeOf, sub_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h
  exact h

/-- The composition relation: `(P, β ∘ α, S) = (P, α, Q) + (Q, β, S)`. -/
theorem of_trans {P Q S : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S) :
    (of ⟨P, S, α ≪≫ β⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = of ⟨P, Q, α⟩ + of ⟨Q, S, β⟩ := by
  have h : (PresentedK0.mk (transRelation T α β) : PresentedK0 (relations T)) = 0 :=
    PresentedK0.mk_eq_zero_of_mem (transRelation_mem_relations T α β)
  rw [transRelation_def, map_sub, map_sub, PresentedK0.mk_freeOf, PresentedK0.mk_freeOf,
    PresentedK0.mk_freeOf, sub_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h
  exact h

/-- The class of an identity triple `(P, id, P)` vanishes. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_refl (P : C) : (of ⟨P, P, Iso.refl _⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = 0 := by
  have h := of_trans (T := T) (Iso.refl (T.obj P)) (Iso.refl _)
  rwa [Iso.refl_trans, left_eq_add] at h

/-- Reversing a triple negates its class: `(Q, α⁻¹, P) = -(P, α, Q)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_symm {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) :
    (of ⟨Q, P, α.symm⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = -of ⟨P, Q, α⟩ := by
  have h := of_trans α α.symm
  rw [Iso.self_symm_id, of_refl] at h
  exact eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_right h.symm

/-- A triple whose isomorphism is the image of an isomorphism of `C` has class zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_mapIso {P Q : C} (γ : P ≅ Q) : (of ⟨P, Q, T.mapIso γ⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = 0 := by
  rw [of_congr (mkIso (x := ⟨P, Q, T.mapIso γ⟩) (y := ⟨Q, Q, Iso.refl _⟩) γ (Iso.refl Q)),
    of_refl]

/-- The classes of triples generate the relative group. -/
theorem closure_range_of : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (of : T ⊡ T → RelativeK0 T)) = ⊤ :=
  PresentedK0.closure_range_of

/-- Induction on the classes of triples. -/
@[elab_as_elim]
theorem induction_on {motive : RelativeK0 T → Prop} (z : RelativeK0 T) (zero : motive 0)
    (of : ∀ x : T ⊡ T, motive (RelativeK0.of x))
    (add : ∀ a b, motive a → motive b → motive (a + b))
    (neg : ∀ a, motive a → motive (-a)) : motive z :=
  PresentedK0.induction_on z zero of add neg

/-- Two homomorphisms out of the relative group agreeing on the classes of triples are equal. -/
@[ext]
theorem hom_ext {G : Type*} [AddMonoid G] {f g : RelativeK0 T →+ G}
    (h : ∀ x : T ⊡ T, f (of x) = g (of x)) : f = g :=
  PresentedK0.hom_ext h

/-- Every element of the relative group is the class of a single triple: sums are direct sums
of triples and negatives are reversed triples. -/
theorem exists_eq_of [HasZeroObject C] (z : RelativeK0 T) : ∃ x : T ⊡ T, z = of x := by
  induction z using induction_on with
  | zero => exact ⟨⟨0, 0, Iso.refl _⟩, (of_refl 0).symm⟩
  | of x => exact ⟨x, rfl⟩
  | add a b ha hb =>
      obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := ha
      obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hb
      exact ⟨tripleBiprod T x y, (of_tripleBiprod x y).symm⟩
  | neg a ha =>
      obtain ⟨⟨P, Q, α⟩, rfl⟩ := ha
      exact ⟨⟨Q, P, α.symm⟩, (of_symm α).symm⟩

section Lift

variable (T) in
/-- An additive invariant for the relative group: a function on triples, constant on isomorphism
classes, additive on direct sums and additive under composition. These are exactly the data that
factor through `TauCeti.RelativeK0 T`; see `TauCeti.RelativeK0.liftEquiv`. -/
@[ext]
structure AdditiveInvariant (G : Type*) [AddCommGroup G] where
  /-- The value of the invariant on a triple. -/
  obj : T ⊡ T → G
  /-- Isomorphic triples receive equal values. -/
  map_iso : ∀ ⦃x y : T ⊡ T⦄, (x ≅ y) → obj x = obj y
  /-- The value on a direct sum of triples is the sum of the values. -/
  map_tripleBiprod : ∀ x y : T ⊡ T, obj (tripleBiprod T x y) = obj x + obj y
  /-- The value on a composite triple is the sum of the values. -/
  map_trans : ∀ {P Q S : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S),
    obj ⟨P, S, α ≪≫ β⟩ = obj ⟨P, Q, α⟩ + obj ⟨Q, S, β⟩

variable {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G]

private noncomputable def AdditiveInvariant.toPresented (a : AdditiveInvariant T G) :
    PresentedK0.AdditiveInvariant (relations T) G where
  obj := a.obj
  map_iso := a.map_iso
  map_rel := by
    rintro _ (⟨x, y, rfl⟩ | ⟨P, Q, S, α, β, rfl⟩)
    · rw [biprodRelation_def, map_sub, map_sub, freeLift_freeOf a.map_iso,
        freeLift_freeOf a.map_iso, freeLift_freeOf a.map_iso, a.map_tripleBiprod]
      abel
    · rw [transRelation_def, map_sub, map_sub, freeLift_freeOf a.map_iso,
        freeLift_freeOf a.map_iso, freeLift_freeOf a.map_iso, a.map_trans, sub_sub, sub_self]

/-- The homomorphism out of the relative group induced by an additive invariant. -/
noncomputable def lift (a : AdditiveInvariant T G) : RelativeK0 T →+ G :=
  PresentedK0.lift a.toPresented

@[simp]
lemma lift_of (a : AdditiveInvariant T G) (x : T ⊡ T) : lift a (of x) = a.obj x :=
  PresentedK0.lift_of a.toPresented x

/-- Any homomorphism agreeing with an additive invariant on the classes of triples is its
induced lift. -/
theorem lift_unique (a : AdditiveInvariant T G) (f : RelativeK0 T →+ G)
    (hf : ∀ x : T ⊡ T, f (of x) = a.obj x) : f = lift a :=
  hom_ext fun x ↦ by rw [hf, lift_of]

/-- The universal property of the relative group: additive invariants with values in `G`
correspond bijectively to additive homomorphisms `RelativeK0 T →+ G`. -/
noncomputable def liftEquiv : AdditiveInvariant T G ≃ (RelativeK0 T →+ G) where
  toFun := lift
  invFun f :=
    { obj := fun x ↦ f (of x)
      map_iso := fun _ _ e ↦ by rw [of_congr e]
      map_tripleBiprod := fun x y ↦ by rw [of_tripleBiprod, map_add]
      map_trans := fun α β ↦ by rw [of_trans, map_add] }
  left_inv a := by ext x; exact lift_of a x
  right_inv f := (lift_unique _ f fun _ ↦ rfl).symm

@[simp]
lemma liftEquiv_apply (a : AdditiveInvariant T G) : liftEquiv a = lift a := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma liftEquiv_symm_apply_obj (f : RelativeK0 T →+ G) (x : T ⊡ T) :
    ((liftEquiv (T := T) (G := G)).symm f).obj x = f (of x) := (rfl)

end Lift

section Difference

variable (T) in
/-- The difference map `K₀(T) → K₀(C)` into the split Grothendieck group of `C`, sending the
class of a triple `(P, α, Q)` to `[P] - [Q]`. -/
noncomputable def toSplitK0 : RelativeK0 T →+ SplitK0 C :=
  lift
    { obj := fun x ↦ SplitK0.of x.fst - SplitK0.of x.snd
      map_iso := fun x y e ↦ by
        have h₁ : SplitK0.of x.fst = SplitK0.of y.fst := SplitK0.of_congr ((π₁ T T).mapIso e)
        have h₂ : SplitK0.of x.snd = SplitK0.of y.snd := SplitK0.of_congr ((π₂ T T).mapIso e)
        rw [h₁, h₂]
      map_tripleBiprod := fun x y ↦ by
        rw [tripleBiprod_fst, tripleBiprod_snd, SplitK0.of_biprod, SplitK0.of_biprod]
        abel
      map_trans := fun _ _ ↦ by abel }

@[simp]
lemma toSplitK0_of (x : T ⊡ T) :
    toSplitK0 T (of x) = SplitK0.of x.fst - SplitK0.of x.snd :=
  lift_of _ x

/-- The composite `K₀(T) → K₀(C) → K₀(D)` of the difference map with the map induced by `T`
vanishes: the two ends of a triple become isomorphic in `D`. -/
theorem splitK0Map_comp_toSplitK0_eq_zero [HasBinaryBiproducts D] [EssentiallySmall.{w'} D] :
    (SplitK0.map T).comp (toSplitK0 T) = 0 :=
  hom_ext fun x ↦ by simp [SplitK0.of_congr x.iso]

@[simp]
lemma splitK0Map_toSplitK0_eq_zero [HasBinaryBiproducts D] [EssentiallySmall.{w'} D]
    (z : RelativeK0 T) : SplitK0.map T (toSplitK0 T z) = 0 :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun splitK0Map_comp_toSplitK0_eq_zero z

end Difference

section FullyFaithful

/-- For a fully faithful functor every triple has class zero, since its isomorphism is the image
of an isomorphism of `C`. -/
theorem of_eq_zero_of_fullyFaithful (hT : T.FullyFaithful) (x : T ⊡ T) :
    (of x : RelativeK0 T) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨P, Q, α⟩ := x
  have h : T.mapIso (hT.preimageIso α) = α := by ext; simp
  rw [← h]
  exact of_mapIso _

/-- The relative group of a fully faithful functor is trivial. -/
theorem subsingleton_of_fullyFaithful (hT : T.FullyFaithful) : Subsingleton (RelativeK0 T) := by
  refine subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun z ↦ ?_
  induction z using induction_on with
  | zero => rfl
  | of x => exact of_eq_zero_of_fullyFaithful hT x
  | add a b ha hb => rw [ha, hb, add_zero]
  | neg a ha => rw [ha, neg_zero]

/-- The relative group of the identity functor is trivial. -/
instance : Subsingleton (RelativeK0 (𝟭 C)) :=
  subsingleton_of_fullyFaithful (Functor.FullyFaithful.id C)

end FullyFaithful

section ZeroTarget

variable (hD : ∀ Y : D, IsZero Y)
include hD

/-- When every object of `D` is zero, triples with isomorphic ends have the same class. -/
private lemma of_eq_of_isZero {x y : T ⊡ T} (e₁ : x.fst ≅ y.fst) (e₂ : x.snd ≅ y.snd) :
    (of x : RelativeK0 T) = of y :=
  of_congr (mkIso e₁ e₂ ((hD _).eq_of_src _ _))

variable [HasZeroObject C]

/-- When every object of `D` is zero, the class map `P ↦ [(P, 0, 0)]` of `C`, the inverse of
the difference map. -/
private noncomputable def ofSplitK0OfIsZero : SplitK0 C →+ RelativeK0 T :=
  SplitK0.lift
    { obj := fun P ↦ of ⟨P, 0, (hD _).iso (hD _)⟩
      map_iso := fun _ _ e ↦ of_eq_of_isZero hD e (Iso.refl _)
      map_biprod := fun P P' ↦ by
        rw [← of_tripleBiprod]
        exact of_eq_of_isZero hD (Iso.refl _) (isoBiprodZero (isZero_zero C)) }

@[simp] private lemma ofSplitK0OfIsZero_of (P : C) :
    ofSplitK0OfIsZero hD (SplitK0.of P) = (of ⟨P, 0, (hD _).iso (hD _)⟩ : RelativeK0 T) :=
  SplitK0.lift_of _ P

/-- When every object of `D` is zero, the difference map is an isomorphism `K₀(T) ≃+ K₀(C)`,
with inverse `[P] ↦ [(P, 0, 0)]`. -/
noncomputable def toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero : RelativeK0 T ≃+ SplitK0 C :=
  AddMonoidHom.toAddEquiv (toSplitK0 T) (ofSplitK0OfIsZero hD)
    (hom_ext fun ⟨P, Q, α⟩ ↦ by
      simp only [AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, toSplitK0_of, map_sub, ofSplitK0OfIsZero_of,
        AddMonoidHom.id_apply]
      rw [sub_eq_add_neg, ← of_symm, ← of_trans]
      exact of_eq_of_isZero hD (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _))
    (SplitK0.hom_ext fun P ↦ by simp)

@[simp]
lemma toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero_apply (z : RelativeK0 T) :
    toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero hD z = toSplitK0 T z := (rfl)

@[simp]
lemma toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero_symm_of (P : C) :
    (toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero hD).symm (SplitK0.of P) =
      (of ⟨P, 0, (hD _).iso (hD _)⟩ : RelativeK0 T) :=
  ofSplitK0OfIsZero_of hD P

end ZeroTarget

end RelativeK0

end Triples

section Triangular

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] {T : C ⥤ D}

namespace RelativeK0

section Commutator

variable [HasZeroMorphisms D] [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T]
  [EssentiallySmall.{w} C] [LocallySmall.{w} D]

open scoped commutatorElement in
/-- The class of a commutator of automorphisms of an object of `D` vanishes, once the object is
identified with an image `T P`: the automorphisms of a fixed `T P` contribute additively. -/
theorem of_trans_commutatorElement_trans {P : C} {W : D} (e : T.obj P ≅ W) (a b : Aut W) :
    (of ⟨P, P, e ≪≫ (⁅a, b⁆ : Aut W).asIso ≪≫ e.symm⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = 0 := by
  have h (x : Aut W) : (of ⟨P, P, e ≪≫ x⁻¹.asIso ≪≫ e.symm⟩ : RelativeK0 T) =
      -of ⟨P, P, e ≪≫ x.asIso ≪≫ e.symm⟩ := by
    rw [← of_symm, show e ≪≫ x⁻¹.asIso ≪≫ e.symm = (e ≪≫ x.asIso ≪≫ e.symm).symm by ext; simp]
  have h' (x y : Aut W) : (of ⟨P, P, e ≪≫ (x * y).asIso ≪≫ e.symm⟩ : RelativeK0 T) =
      of ⟨P, P, e ≪≫ x.asIso ≪≫ e.symm⟩ + of ⟨P, P, e ≪≫ y.asIso ≪≫ e.symm⟩ := by
    rw [add_comm, ← of_trans, show e ≪≫ (x * y).asIso ≪≫ e.symm =
      (e ≪≫ y.asIso ≪≫ e.symm) ≪≫ (e ≪≫ x.asIso ≪≫ e.symm) by ext; simp]
  rw [commutatorElement_def, h', h', h', h, h]
  abel

end Commutator

variable [Preadditive D] [HasBinaryBiproducts D] [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms]
  [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T] [EssentiallySmall.{w} C] [LocallySmall.{w} D]

open scoped commutatorElement in
/-- An automorphism of `T (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)` which fixes `T` of the first inclusion and induces the
identity along `T` of the second projection has trivial class, whatever its off-diagonal block:
after adding the identity triple on `Q₂` it becomes a commutator. -/
theorem of_eq_zero_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq {Q₁ Q₂ : C}
    {u : T.obj (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ≅ T.obj (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)}
    (h₁ : T.map biprod.inl ≫ u.hom = T.map biprod.inl)
    (h₂ : u.hom ≫ T.map biprod.snd = T.map biprod.snd) :
    (of ⟨Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, u⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = 0 := by
  have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
  set M := T.mapBiprod Q₁ Q₂
  -- Add the identity triple on `Q₂` and identify `T ((Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ⊞ Q₂)` with
  -- `(T Q₁ ⊞ T Q₂) ⊞ T Q₂`, where `u ⊞ 𝟙` becomes a commutator.
  set E : T.obj ((Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ⊞ Q₂) ≅ (T.obj Q₁ ⊞ T.obj Q₂) ⊞ T.obj Q₂ :=
    T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂ ≪≫ biprod.mapIso M (Iso.refl _)
  have h : T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂ ≪≫ biprod.mapIso u (Iso.refl _) ≪≫
      (T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂).symm =
      E ≪≫ (Aut.of (biprod.mapIso (M.symm ≪≫ u ≪≫ M) (Iso.refl _))).asIso ≪≫ E.symm := by
    have hu : biprod.mapIso u (Iso.refl (T.obj Q₂)) = biprod.mapIso M (Iso.refl _) ≪≫
        biprod.mapIso (M.symm ≪≫ u ≪≫ M) (Iso.refl _) ≪≫ (biprod.mapIso M (Iso.refl _)).symm := by
      ext <;> simp
    rw [hu]
    simp only [E, Iso.trans_symm, Iso.trans_assoc]
  have h' : (of ⟨(Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ⊞ Q₂, (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ⊞ Q₂, T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂ ≪≫
      biprod.mapIso u (Iso.refl _) ≪≫ (T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂).symm⟩ : RelativeK0 T) =
      of ⟨Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, u⟩ + of ⟨Q₂, Q₂, Iso.refl _⟩ :=
    of_tripleBiprod ⟨Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, u⟩ ⟨Q₂, Q₂, Iso.refl _⟩
  rw [of_refl, add_zero, h, T.mapBiprod_symm_trans_trans_eq_unipotentLower u h₁ h₂,
    Biprod.unipotentLower_biprod_eq_commutatorElement, of_trans_commutatorElement_trans] at h'
  exact h'.symm

/-- The relation for triangular isomorphisms: if `γ : T (P₁ ⊞ P₂) ≅ T (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)` restricts to
`α₁` along `T` of the first inclusions and induces `α₂` along `T` of the second projections, then
`(P₁ ⊞ P₂, γ, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) = (P₁, α₁, Q₁) + (P₂, α₂, Q₂)`, whatever its off-diagonal block
`T P₂ ⟶ T Q₁`. This is the relation imposed by a split short exact sequence of triples. -/
theorem of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq {P₁ P₂ Q₁ Q₂ : C} {α₁ : T.obj P₁ ≅ T.obj Q₁}
    {α₂ : T.obj P₂ ≅ T.obj Q₂} {γ : T.obj (P₁ ⊞ P₂) ≅ T.obj (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)}
    (h₁ : T.map biprod.inl ≫ γ.hom = α₁.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inl)
    (h₂ : γ.hom ≫ T.map biprod.snd = T.map biprod.snd ≫ α₂.hom) :
    (of ⟨P₁ ⊞ P₂, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, γ⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = of ⟨P₁, Q₁, α₁⟩ + of ⟨P₂, Q₂, α₂⟩ := by
  have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T
  set δ := T.mapBiprod P₁ P₂ ≪≫ biprod.mapIso α₁ α₂ ≪≫ (T.mapBiprod Q₁ Q₂).symm
  have hδ : (of ⟨P₁ ⊞ P₂, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂, δ⟩ : RelativeK0 T) = of ⟨P₁, Q₁, α₁⟩ + of ⟨P₂, Q₂, α₂⟩ :=
    of_tripleBiprod ⟨P₁, Q₁, α₁⟩ ⟨P₂, Q₂, α₂⟩
  have hδ₁ : T.map biprod.inl ≫ δ.inv = α₁.inv ≫ T.map biprod.inl := by simp [δ]
  have hδ₂ : δ.inv ≫ T.map biprod.snd = T.map biprod.snd ≫ α₂.inv := by simp [δ]
  have hγ : γ = δ ≪≫ (δ.symm ≪≫ γ) := by simp
  rw [hγ, of_trans, hδ, of_eq_zero_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq (u := δ.symm ≪≫ γ), add_zero]
  · simp [reassoc_of% hδ₁, h₁]
  · simp [h₂, reassoc_of% hδ₂]

end RelativeK0

end Triangular

section TripleMap

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D]
  {C' : Type u''} [Category.{v''} C'] {D' : Type u'''} [Category.{v'''} D']
  {T : C ⥤ D} {T' : C' ⥤ D'} (F : C ⥤ C') (G : D ⥤ D') (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T')

namespace RelativeK0

/-- The functor between categories of triples induced by functors `F : C ⥤ C'` and `G : D ⥤ D'`
and a natural isomorphism `e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T'`: it sends `(P, α, Q)` to
`(F P, e_Q ∘ G α ∘ e_P⁻¹, F Q)`. -/
-- The body is exposed: the type of the isomorphism of the image of a triple depends on its two
-- ends, so stating its formula needs the ends of the image definitionally.
@[expose, simps]
def tripleMap : T ⊡ T ⥤ T' ⊡ T' where
  obj x := ⟨F.obj x.fst, F.obj x.snd, (e.app x.fst).symm ≪≫ G.mapIso x.iso ≪≫ e.app x.snd⟩
  map f :=
    { fst := F.map f.fst
      snd := F.map f.snd
      w := by
        have h₁ := e.inv.naturality f.fst
        have h₂ := e.hom.naturality f.snd
        dsimp at h₁ h₂ ⊢
        rw [reassoc_of% h₁, ← G.map_comp_assoc, f.w, G.map_comp_assoc, h₂]
        simp only [Category.assoc] }

end RelativeK0

end TripleMap

section Functoriality

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [HasZeroMorphisms D]
  {C' : Type u''} [Category.{v''} C'] [HasZeroMorphisms C'] [HasBinaryBiproducts C']
  {D' : Type u'''} [Category.{v'''} D'] [HasZeroMorphisms D']
  {T : C ⥤ D} [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T]
  {T' : C' ⥤ D'} [T'.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T']
  (F : C ⥤ C') (G : D ⥤ D') (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T')

namespace RelativeK0

variable [F.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F]

/-- The functor of triples carries direct sums of triples to direct sums, through the
identifications `F (X ⊞ Y) ≅ F X ⊞ F Y`. -/
private noncomputable def tripleMapTripleBiprodIso (x y : T ⊡ T) :
    (tripleMap F G e).obj (tripleBiprod T x y) ≅
      tripleBiprod T' ((tripleMap F G e).obj x) ((tripleMap F G e).obj y) :=
  letI := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts F
  letI := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts T'
  mkIso (F.mapBiprod _ _) (F.mapBiprod _ _) (by
    -- Compare both sides after the images under `T'` of the two projections, moving `e` past the
    -- projections by naturality.
    dsimp only [tripleBiprod, tripleMap]
    refine Functor.map_biprod_hom_ext ?_ ?_ <;>
      simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, biprod.mapIso_hom,
        Functor.mapIso_hom, Iso.app_hom, Iso.app_inv, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst,
        Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd, biprod.map_fst, biprod.map_snd, ← T'.map_comp_assoc,
        ← T'.map_comp, Functor.mapBiprod_hom, biprod.lift_fst, biprod.lift_snd,
        biprod.lift_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_snd_assoc]
      <;> simp only [← Functor.comp_map, e.inv.naturality_assoc, ← e.hom.naturality]
      <;> simp only [Functor.comp_map, ← G.map_comp_assoc, Category.assoc,
        Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_fst, Functor.mapBiprod_inv_map_snd, biprod.map_fst,
        biprod.map_snd, biprod.lift_fst_assoc, biprod.lift_snd_assoc])

variable [EssentiallySmall.{w} C] [LocallySmall.{w} D] [EssentiallySmall.{w'} C']
  [LocallySmall.{w'} D']

private lemma freeMap_relations_mem_closure :
    ∀ r ∈ relations T, freeMap (tripleMap F G e) r ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (relations T') := by
  rintro _ (⟨x, y, rfl⟩ | ⟨P, Q, S, α, β, rfl⟩)
  · rw [biprodRelation_def, map_sub, map_sub, freeMap_freeOf, freeMap_freeOf, freeMap_freeOf,
      freeOf_congr (tripleMapTripleBiprodIso F G e x y)]
    exact AddSubgroup.subset_closure (biprodRelation_mem_relations _ _ _)
  · have h : (tripleMap F G e).obj ⟨P, S, α ≪≫ β⟩ = ⟨F.obj P, F.obj S,
        ((tripleMap F G e).obj ⟨P, Q, α⟩).iso ≪≫ ((tripleMap F G e).obj ⟨Q, S, β⟩).iso⟩ := by
      refine congrArg (CategoricalPullback.mk (F := T') (G := T') (F.obj P) (F.obj S)) ?_
      ext
      dsimp only [tripleMap]
      simp
    rw [transRelation_def, map_sub, map_sub, freeMap_freeOf, freeMap_freeOf, freeMap_freeOf, h]
    exact AddSubgroup.subset_closure (transRelation_mem_relations _ _ _)

/-- The homomorphism `K₀(T) → K₀(T')` induced by functors `F : C ⥤ C'` and `G : D ⥤ D'` and a
natural isomorphism `e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T'`, sending `[(P, α, Q)]` to
`[(F P, e_Q ∘ G α ∘ e_P⁻¹, F Q)]`. -/
noncomputable def map : RelativeK0 T →+ RelativeK0 T' :=
  PresentedK0.map (tripleMap F G e) (freeMap_relations_mem_closure F G e)

@[simp]
lemma map_of (x : T ⊡ T) : map F G e (of x) = of ((tripleMap F G e).obj x) :=
  PresentedK0.map_of _ _ x

/-- The difference maps are natural: the map induced by a commuting square, followed by the
difference map of `T'`, is the difference map of `T` followed by the map induced by `F`. -/
theorem toSplitK0_comp_map :
    (toSplitK0 T').comp (map F G e) = (SplitK0.map F).comp (toSplitK0 T) :=
  hom_ext fun x ↦ by simp

@[simp]
lemma toSplitK0_map (z : RelativeK0 T) :
    toSplitK0 T' (map F G e z) = SplitK0.map F (toSplitK0 T z) :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (toSplitK0_comp_map F G e) z

/-- The identity square, with the unitors `T ⋙ 𝟭 D ≅ T ≅ 𝟭 C ⋙ T`, induces the identity of
`K₀(T)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_id : map (𝟭 C) (𝟭 D) (T.rightUnitor ≪≫ T.leftUnitor.symm) =
    AddMonoidHom.id (RelativeK0 T) :=
  hom_ext fun x ↦ by
    rw [map_of, AddMonoidHom.id_apply]
    exact of_congr (mkIso (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (by dsimp only [tripleMap]; simp))

end RelativeK0

end Functoriality

section FunctorialityComp

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [HasZeroMorphisms D]
  {C' : Type u''} [Category.{v''} C'] [HasZeroMorphisms C'] [HasBinaryBiproducts C']
  {D' : Type u'''} [Category.{v'''} D'] [HasZeroMorphisms D']
  {C'' : Type u₅} [Category.{v₅} C''] [HasZeroMorphisms C''] [HasBinaryBiproducts C'']
  {D'' : Type u₆} [Category.{v₆} D''] [HasZeroMorphisms D'']
  {T : C ⥤ D} [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T]
  {T' : C' ⥤ D'} [T'.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T']
  {T'' : C'' ⥤ D''} [T''.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair T'']
  (F : C ⥤ C') (G : D ⥤ D') (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T')
  [F.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F]
  (F' : C' ⥤ C'') (G' : D' ⥤ D'') (e' : T' ⋙ G' ≅ F' ⋙ T'')
  [F'.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F']
  [EssentiallySmall.{w} C] [LocallySmall.{w} D] [EssentiallySmall.{w'} C'] [LocallySmall.{w'} D']
  [EssentiallySmall.{w''} C''] [LocallySmall.{w''} D'']

namespace RelativeK0

/-- The maps induced by commuting squares compose: the vertically pasted square of `(F, G, e)` and
`(F', G', e')`, whose isomorphism is that of Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.CatCommSq.vComp`, induces
the composite of the two maps. -/
theorem map_comp :
    map (F ⋙ F') (G ⋙ G') ((Functor.associator _ _ _).symm ≪≫ Functor.isoWhiskerRight e G' ≪≫
      Functor.associator _ _ _ ≪≫ Functor.isoWhiskerLeft F e' ≪≫ (Functor.associator _ _ _).symm) =
      (map F' G' e').comp (map F G e) :=
  hom_ext fun x ↦ by
    rw [AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, map_of, map_of, map_of]
    exact of_congr (mkIso (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (by dsimp only [tripleMap]; simp))

end RelativeK0

end FunctorialityComp

